generation_sheets.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve.
The reference is the approved QuietTraveler game sprite turnaround. Create a production WALK-CYCLE SPRITE SHEET of exactly the SAME male character. Preserve the reference's proportions, face, short dark blue-gray hair, desaturated blue-teal cape with silver clasp, cream tunic, charcoal trousers, brown boots, and small brown satchel. Same crisp fine sprite detail, selective dark outlines and soft cel shading. This is an animated character sheet, not concept art.
Output EXACTLY 16 full-body sprites in a precisely aligned 4 columns x 4 rows equal grid, square 2048x2048 transparent canvas. Each cell 512x512. Each character approximately 400 pixels tall, centered with generous transparent margins, consistent scale and ground baseline. NO grid lines, NO labels, NO text, NO backdrop, NO ground or cast shadow. Transparent alpha exactly zero in empty areas; no glows or vignettes.
There are TWO separate 8-frame looping WALK cycles. Frame order left-to-right then next row:
ROWS 1 and 2 = SOUTH: straight toward the viewer, full front. ALL eight sprites in these rows keep this same facing.
ROWS 3 and 4 = NORTH: straight away from viewer, full BACK, NO face visible. ALL eight sprites in these rows keep this same facing.
For each cycle, the eight consecutive poses are:
0 left leg stepping forward, right leg behind, opposite arms swinging;
1 weight settles onto left foot, right heel lifts;
2 right leg passes underneath body, left foot supports;
3 right knee swings forward, left leg starts to trail;
4 right leg stepping forward, left leg behind, opposite arms swinging (the opposite of frame0);
5 weight settles onto right foot, left heel lifts;
6 left leg passes underneath body, right foot supports;
7 left knee swings forward, right leg starts to trail, smoothly leads into frame0.
A restrained calm natural walk in place: obvious alternating leg movement, small arm counter-swing, subtle cape and satchel sway. No running, no jumping, no crouching. Feet must show stepping variation across all 8 frames, not eight repeated standing poses. Torso stays upright, head and body identity/size consistent. Hands empty.
Maintain satchel on the same anatomical LEFT hip, strap across torso from right shoulder, correctly occluded by torso/cape in appropriate views. Never rotate head toward viewer during back views. Keep each whole head and boot comfortably inside its own cell. Camera fixed orthographic low top-down, as reference.

